
Affix_Allocator
Cascading allocator (What would this do?)
Logarithmic Bucketizer

Add caching allocators.
    These would ask another allocator for memory and hold an internal memory cache.
    Allows splitting memory from large block allocators to satisfy small allocations.

Find a reason to use Bucketizers

Add allocator types for multithreading
    - Thread-local allocator
    - Thread-caching allocator
    - Cpu-arena allocator
    - Queueing allocator (this one would queue requests that can't be satisfied at the moment they arrive)

Add fragmentation and ussage stats computation functions for allocators.

Add hash specialization for memory block structures

Add NEW CLASS of allocators that actively allocate and deallocate auxiliary memory. I would cal them "dynamic allocators". While they all do dynamic allocation, this allocators would also be dynamic themselves.
This enables the use of variable-size memory structures in allocators.
***This kind of allocators cannot exist on they own, as they need a previously existing allocator to get memory dynamically.

ScopedAllocator: automatically calls deallocate for all memory allocated through its lifetime

See alignment issues
